# transfer archives - a zip is how something got from one machine to another,
# never a source artefact
*.zip

# build output
build/
plugin/dist/
bin/
obj/
*.o
*.elf
*.bin
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# captures are local fixtures, not source
captures/**/*.ndjson

# SimHub property inventories are NOT committed.
#
# They dump every property with its live value, which is what made them good evidence and what
# makes them unpublishable: iRacing's session data names every driver on track and carries their
# customer IDs, third-party plugins republish those names under their own property trees, and the
# telemetry-file path contains the operator's account name. Redacting that reliably means
# enumerating fields that plugins are free to name however they like - it was attempted twice and
# was wrong both times, once too narrow and once so broad it destroyed the evidence.
#
# Nothing is lost by excluding them. FINDINGS.md records every mapping row with its observed value,
# and summary.txt records the distinct-value answers. Keep the raw files locally if you want them.
captures/**/properties-inventory*.txt

# never commit secrets
*.local
secrets.*

# SimHub's own assemblies, referenced at build time with Private="False" and NEVER redistributed.
# POLICY-NO-REDISTRIBUTION-SIMHUB; check G3 asserts no release artefact contains them.
plugin/lib/*.dll
